[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.
#1: Setup equipment:
a. Enter operator initials.
b. Enter serial number into the box above.
DISPLAY: PCB 287-027.png
CLICK_OK:

#2: Setup equipment1:
a. Set adjustable PSU output 1 to 12V ±0.1V, 1.5A ±0.1A. Switch the output off.
b. Using TE159, connect the PSU to the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).
c. Connect the PC (via USB) to the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).
d. Connect the USB cable to the K5 on the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).
DISPLAY: TE192Setup.jpg
CLICK_OK:

#3: Setup equipment:
a. Connect the MLPRO 2 Test Box (TE194) to the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).  
b. Using the 20-way ribbon cable connect the PCB to the TE192 Test box.
c. Connect the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086) to the PC and place the PCB inside.
d. Switch the output of the adjustable PSU on and power on the TE132 Peripheral lighting PCB Test Jig. 
DISPLAY: 1ringlightSetup.jpg
COMMENT: *Example image below*
CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: MLPRO2 
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#										// turn off any LEDs still on: 
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #2


#4: PCB communication check
COMMAND: MLPRO2  BENUM
READLINE: MLPRO2  BENUM
Returned result is = %BENUM%
IF: %BENUM% STR_EQ RS,RS1,RS2, 							//  a correct expected Return result 
GOTO: #4.1: 
.
The returned result is NOT as exected, investigate the fault and click RETRY to repeat the test.
.
.
The expected result is = BL1,BL2,BR1,BR2,FL1,FL2,FR1,FR2,RS,RS1,RS2, 
IMPORTANT: Test has FAILED                Test has FAILED                   Test has FAILED                   Test has FAILED
COMMENT: If you want to continue fault-finding the rest of the PCB, click on ‘Skip’
SKIP_FAIL: #4
GOTO: #5

#4.1: PCB communication check - test passed
TEST: PASSED
COMMENT: Test passed
CLICK_OK:
EXE: OpenWinCam.bat


#5: RING LIGHT LED  = RED
a. Check for 4 LED hot spots
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 100000 650
DELAY: 750
PASS_FAIL: #5

#6: RING LIGHT LED = BLUEGREEN
a. Check for 4 LED hot spots
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 001000 650
DELAY: 700
PASS_FAIL: #6

#7: RING LIGHT LED = VIOLET
a. Check for 4 LED hot spots
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 000010 650
DELAY: 700
PASS_FAIL: #7

#8: RING LIGHT LED = UV
a. Check for 4 LED hot spots
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 000001 650
DELAY: 700
PASS_FAIL: #8

#9: RING LIGHT LED = GREEN
a. Check for 4 LED hot spots
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 010000 650
DELAY: 700
PASS_FAIL: #9

#10: RING LIGHT LED = BLUE
a. Check for 4 LED hot spots
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 000100 650
DELAY: 700
PASS_FAIL: #10

#11: Full load test - 4 output on at the same time 
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 001111 1023
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: MLPRO2 READAMPS
READLINE: MLPRO2 READAMPS
Returned Version is = %READAMPS%
RANGE: %READAMPS% 875 50					// value range 900-1000
IF:											// if value is between range then goto
GOTO: #11.1: 
The returned result is NOT as exected, investigate the fault and click RETRY to repeat the test.
.
.
The expected result is =  greater than 10V 
IMPORTANT: Test has FAILED                Test has FAILED                   Test has FAILED                   Test has FAILED
COMMENT: If you want to continue fault-finding the rest of the PCB, click on ‘Skip’
SKIP_FAIL: #11
GOTO: #12

#11.1: PCB communication check - test passed
TEST: PASSED
test passed
CLICK_OK:


#12: Test complete:
EXE: CloseWinCam.bat
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and then power off the PSU and disconnect the PCB.
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
EXE: CloseWinCam.bat
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
DISCONNECT: MLPRO2

